 {"id":"fabro-b3c1","title":"web: typecheck must cover test files — tsconfig exclude hides test-file type errors from CI","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-06T09:46:11.576Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:41.858Z","description":"apps/fabro-web/tsconfig.json excludes **/*.test.ts and **/*.test.tsx, so 'bun run typecheck' (tsc) never checks test files while editors (VS Code TS server) DO surface their errors — observed 2026-09-06 with automations.test.tsx (teardown misuse + unknown-typed mock body): bun tests passed, typecheck green, user saw type errors in the editor. SECOND INSTANCE same day (PR #32 gate): the editor's NEWER TypeScript service offered a quick-fix 'ignoreDeprecations: 6.0' for a deprecation only TS 6.x knows; the value breaks CI's tsc 5.9 (TS5103) — editor and project TypeScript versions diverge. Fix: (a) typecheck-tests script/config (tsconfig without the exclude, bun-types for bun:test) wired into CI/typecheck so editor and CI agree; (b) pin the editor to the workspace TypeScript via .vscode/settings.json 'typescript.tsdk': 'node_modules/typescript/lib' so quick-fixes match CI; (c) then fix any pre-existing test-file type errors the widened check uncovers.","labels":["web","ci"],"assignee":"fabro"}
